<!--
  The themed-icon layer: the mark ALONE, as a silhouette on transparency.

  A launcher tints this whole drawable one colour and reads only its alpha, so it must not carry
  the logo's rounded plate. With the plate in it, plate and mark tint to the same colour and the
  icon renders as a single solid block with no mark visible (#87).

  Dropping the plate means the mark can no longer be sized to sit inside it: at the foreground
  layer's 0.49 it would cover barely a third of the canvas and read as shrunken next to its
  neighbours. At 0.78 it spans about 57dp of the 108dp canvas, comfortably inside the 72dp region
  an adaptive mask never clips, and keeps the breathing room the coloured icon has around its own
  mark. The translate centres the mark's OWN bounds, which sit a little above and left of the
  viewport centre, rather than centring the viewport, so it changes whenever the scale does.

  The fill colour only has to be opaque, since a tint keeps nothing but the alpha; white is the
  convention.
  -->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="192"
    android:viewportHeight="192">
  <group android:scaleX="0.78"
      android:scaleY="0.78"
      android:translateX="21.97"
      android:translateY="22.42">
